VALUES
  ('NCLEX_TUT_MCQ_00201', '4ed777d7-e4f7-403b-88f4-63ce5432d65e', 'MCQ',
   'A client''s last menstrual period began on 10 June. Using Naegele''s rule, what is her estimated date of delivery?',
   'Naegele''s rule: take the FIRST day of the last menstrual period, add 7 days, subtract 3 months. 10 June + 7 days = 17 June; 17 June minus 3 months = 17 March.',
   $j${"options": [{"id": "A", "text": "17 March"}, {"id": "B", "text": "3 March"}, {"id": "C", "text": "17 September"}, {"id": "D", "text": "10 March"}]}$j$::jsonb,
   $j${"answer": "A", "feedback": {"A": "Correct — add 7 days first, then subtract 3 months.", "B": "Incorrect — the 7 days were not added.", "C": "Incorrect — 3 months were added rather than subtracted.", "D": "Incorrect — the 7 days were not added."}}$j$::jsonb,
   'Maternity', 'Naegele''s rule', 'Easy',
   ARRAY['maternity', 'dating']::text[], 1, '75000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000001'),
  ('NCLEX_TUT_MCQ_00202', '4ed777d7-e4f7-403b-88f4-63ce5432d65e', 'MCQ',
   'A client is 28 weeks pregnant and has gained 22 lb. What is the nurse''s best interpretation?',
   'The shortcut is weeks of gestation minus 9: 28 - 9 = 19 lb expected. She is 3 lb over. A variance of 1-2 lb is normal, 3 lb warrants assessment, and 4 lb or more suggests real trouble and a biophysical profile.',
   $j${"options": [{"id": "A", "text": "Within normal limits — no action needed"}, {"id": "B", "text": "About 3 lb above the expected gain — assess the client"}, {"id": "C", "text": "About 8 lb above the expected gain — a biophysical profile is indicated"}, {"id": "D", "text": "Below the expected gain — assess for undernutrition"}]}$j$::jsonb,
   $j${"answer": "B", "feedback": {"A": "Incorrect — 3 lb over is outside the 1-2 lb normal band.", "B": "Correct — 22 against an expected 19. Assess.", "C": "Incorrect — that threshold is 4 lb or more.", "D": "Incorrect — she has gained more than expected, not less."}}$j$::jsonb,
   'Maternity', 'Weight gain', 'Medium',
   ARRAY['maternity', 'dating']::text[], 1, '75000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000001'),
  ('NCLEX_TUT_TF_00201', '4ed777d7-e4f7-403b-88f4-63ce5432d65e', 'TF',
   'Fundal height can be palpated abdominally before 12 weeks'' gestation.',
   'The fundus cannot be palpated abdominally until about week 12, when it sits midway between the symphysis pubis and the umbilicus. It reaches the umbilicus at 20-22 weeks.',
   $j${"options": [{"id": "A", "text": "True"}, {"id": "B", "text": "False"}]}$j$::jsonb,
   $j${"answer": "B", "feedback": {"A": "Incorrect — before 12 weeks the uterus is still behind the symphysis.", "B": "Correct — 12 weeks is the earliest it can be felt."}}$j$::jsonb,
   'Maternity', 'Fundal height', 'Easy',
   ARRAY['maternity', 'dating']::text[], 1, '75000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000001'),
  ('NCLEX_TUT_MCQ_00203', '4ed777d7-e4f7-403b-88f4-63ce5432d65e', 'MCQ',
   'A client attends her 12-week prenatal visit. When should the nurse schedule the next one?',
   'Monthly until 28 weeks, fortnightly from 28 to 36 weeks, then weekly from 36 weeks until delivery or week 42, whichever comes first. At 12 weeks she is still in the monthly phase.',
   $j${"options": [{"id": "A", "text": "In one week"}, {"id": "B", "text": "In two weeks"}, {"id": "C", "text": "In four weeks"}, {"id": "D", "text": "In six weeks"}]}$j$::jsonb,
   $j${"answer": "C", "feedback": {"A": "Incorrect — weekly visits start at 36 weeks.", "B": "Incorrect — fortnightly visits start at 28 weeks.", "C": "Correct — monthly until 28 weeks.", "D": "Incorrect — the interval never stretches to six weeks."}}$j$::jsonb,
   'Maternity', 'Prenatal schedule', 'Easy',
   ARRAY['maternity', 'dating']::text[], 1, '75000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000001'),
  ('NCLEX_TUT_SATA_00201', '4ed777d7-e4f7-403b-88f4-63ce5432d65e', 'SATA',
   'Which findings are POSITIVE signs of pregnancy? Select all that apply.',
   'A positive sign is one only the fetus can produce and only an examiner can verify. hCG can be raised by other conditions including cancer, and movement felt by the MOTHER is subjective — it is the examiner palpating it that counts.',
   $j${"options": [{"id": "A", "text": "Fetal skeleton visible on x-ray"}, {"id": "B", "text": "A positive urine hCG test"}, {"id": "C", "text": "Fetus visible on ultrasound"}, {"id": "D", "text": "Fetal heart heard on Doppler"}, {"id": "E", "text": "The examiner palpates fetal movement"}, {"id": "F", "text": "The mother reports feeling the baby move"}]}$j$::jsonb,
   $j${"answers": ["A", "C", "D", "E"], "feedback": {"A": "Correct — only a fetus has a fetal skeleton.", "B": "Incorrect — hCG rises in other conditions too. Probable, not positive.", "C": "Correct.", "D": "Correct.", "E": "Correct — examiner-palpated movement is objective.", "F": "Incorrect — the mother's report is subjective. Quickening is presumptive."}}$j$::jsonb,
   'Maternity', 'Signs of pregnancy', 'Medium',
   ARRAY['maternity', 'signs']::text[], 4, '75000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000002'),
  ('NCLEX_TUT_MCQ_00204', '4ed777d7-e4f7-403b-88f4-63ce5432d65e', 'MCQ',
   'Which sign is the softening of the cervix?',
   'The three run in alphabetical order and travel upward through the anatomy: Chadwick (bluish discoloration of vulva, vagina and cervix), Goodell (cervix goes soft — Goodell, good and soft), Hegar (lower uterine segment softens).',
   $j${"options": [{"id": "A", "text": "Chadwick's sign"}, {"id": "B", "text": "Goodell's sign"}, {"id": "C", "text": "Hegar's sign"}, {"id": "D", "text": "Braxton Hicks"}]}$j$::jsonb,
   $j${"answer": "B", "feedback": {"A": "Incorrect — Chadwick's is the bluish colour change.", "B": "Correct — Goodell, good and soft.", "C": "Incorrect — Hegar's is softening of the lower uterine segment.", "D": "Incorrect — Braxton Hicks are practice contractions."}}$j$::jsonb,
   'Maternity', 'Signs of pregnancy', 'Easy',
   ARRAY['maternity', 'signs']::text[], 1, '75000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000002')
